    "semantic_summary": "* SetDevicePalette: load a device colour table through the GDI Escape\n * interface.  The driver is first asked (QUERYESCSUPPORT, 8) whether it\n * supports SETCOLORTABLE (4, held in a stack word); if not, 0 is\n * returned.  A null colour pointer resets the device table with an\n * empty SETCOLORTABLE.  Otherwise a 0x42-byte stack table (first index,\n * count, up to sixteen COLORREF entries built with the RGB packing from\n * the far 4-byte palette entries, whose segment is kept in DS for the\n * loop) is sent with SETCOLORTABLE.  The escape word doubles as the loop\n * counter.  1 is returned.",
    "binding_evidence": [
      "Candidate declarations and source comments; inspect packet bindings before acceptance"
    ],
    "publics": [
      "_SetDevicePalette"
    ]
  },
